---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site, links } from '../lib/site';
import aboutBg from '../assets/aboutbg.webp';

const description =
	'How to stop antivirus software, Windows Defender and ransomware protection from blocking PollyMC-Continued downloads ("Permission denied" errors).';
---

<Layout
	title="Antivirus Guide"
	description={description}
	canonical={`${site.url}/antivirus/`}
	background={aboutBg}
>
	<main id="main" class="container">
		<div class="content">
			<h1 class="sec-h">Antivirus Guide</h1>
			<div class="feature-subs">
				<p>
					Sometimes antivirus software, Windows ransomware protection or a cloud-sync
					client blocks PollyMC-Continued while it writes game files. When that
					happens, downloads fail with <code>Permission denied</code> and the launcher shows
					the network error window. This page shows how to fix it.
				</p>
			</div>
			<nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page">
				<a href="#quick-fix">Quick fix</a>
				<a href="#defender">Windows Defender</a>
				<a href="#ransomware">Ransomware protection</a>
				<a href="#other-av">Other antivirus</a>
				<a href="#still-failing">Still failing?</a>
			</nav>
		</div>

		<div class="infobox guide reveal" id="quick-fix">
			<h1>Quick fix: use another temporary folder</h1>
			<p>
				Does the error window say <em>"This looks like antivirus software…"</em>? You can
				retry without touching your antivirus settings:
			</p>
			<ol>
				<li>In the error window, choose the option to retry through a different temporary folder.</li>
				<li>
					Pick a folder your antivirus does not watch, such as a folder in your home
					directory.
				</li>
				<li>The failed downloads run again and are staged in that folder.</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="guide-note">
				If this works, you are done. If you keep seeing the same error, add exclusions using the steps below.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="infobox guide reveal" id="defender">
			<h1>Windows Defender exclusions</h1>
			<p>
				Exclude both the launcher folder and its data folder, so Defender stops scanning
				files while they are being written.
			</p>
			<ol>
				<li>Open <strong>Windows Security</strong> from the Start menu.</li>
				<li>Go to <strong>Virus &amp; threat protection</strong>, then under <em>Virus &amp; threat protection settings</em> click <strong>Manage settings</strong>.</li>
				<li>Scroll down to <strong>Exclusions</strong> and click <strong>Add or remove exclusions</strong>.</li>
				<li>Click <strong>Add an exclusion</strong> → <strong>Folder</strong> and add each folder from the table below.</li>
			</ol>

			<div class="guide-table-wrap">
				<table class="guide-table">
					<thead>
						<tr><th>What</th><th>Default location</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Installed launcher (installer)</td>
							<td><code>C:\Program Files\PollyMC-Continued</code></td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Launcher data (instances, mods, settings)</td>
							<td><code>%APPDATA%\PollyMC</code></td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Portable version</td>
							<td>The folder you extracted the <code>.zip</code> into</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="guide-note">
				Tip: paste <code>%APPDATA%\PollyMC</code> into the File Explorer address bar to jump straight to the data folder.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="infobox guide reveal" id="ransomware">
			<h1>Ransomware protection (Controlled folder access)</h1>
			<p>
				If you use Controlled folder access, Windows can block <code>pollymc.exe</code> from
				writing into protected folders such as Documents, even when Defender exclusions are set.
				Allow the launcher through it:
			</p>
			<ol>
				<li>Open <strong>Windows Security</strong> → <strong>Virus &amp; threat protection</strong>.</li>
				<li>Under <em>Ransomware protection</em>, click <strong>Manage ransomware protection</strong>.</li>
				<li>Click <strong>Allow an app through Controlled folder access</strong>.</li>
				<li>Choose <strong>Add an allowed app</strong> → <strong>Browse all apps</strong> and select <code>pollymc.exe</code> from the launcher folder.</li>
			</ol>
		</div>

		<div class="infobox guide reveal" id="other-av">
			<h1>Other antivirus programs</h1>
			<p>
				Every antivirus names things differently, but the idea is the same. Look for a setting called
				<strong>Exclusions</strong>, <strong>Exceptions</strong>, <strong>Trusted applications</strong> or
				<strong>Allow list</strong>, then add:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>The launcher folder, or at least <code>pollymc.exe</code></li>
				<li>The launcher data folder (<code>%APPDATA%\PollyMC</code>)</li>
				<li>Your Minecraft/Java folders, if the program also blocks the game itself</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Cloud-sync clients (OneDrive, Dropbox, Google Drive) can also lock files. If your launcher
				data lives inside a synced folder, move it out or pause syncing while downloading.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="infobox guide reveal" id="still-failing">
			<h1>Still not working?</h1>
			<p>
				Make sure the launcher is installed from the official <a href="/downloads/">downloads page</a>,
				then restart it and retry the download. If the error keeps coming back, tell us:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Ask in our <a href={links.discord} rel="noopener">Discord server</a>.</li>
				<li>Or open an issue on <a href={links.github} rel="noopener">GitHub</a> and include the launcher log.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				<a class="button is-big" href="/downloads/">Back to Downloads</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.guide-toc {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.5em;
		margin-top: 1em;
	}
	.guide-toc a {
		background: var(--accent);
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 0.4em 0.9em;
		text-decoration: none;
		color: var(--primary-text);
		font-size: 0.95em;
		transition: background 0.15s ease;
	}
	.guide-toc a:hover,
	.guide-toc a:focus {
		background: var(--accent-light);
	}
	.guide {
		scroll-margin-top: 1em;
		padding-bottom: 1.25em;
	}
	.guide p,
	.guide li {
		font-size: 1.1em;
		line-height: 1.6;
		opacity: 0.92;
	}
	.guide ol,
	.guide ul {
		padding-left: 1.4em;
		margin: 0.6em 0;
	}
	.guide li {
		padding: 0.2em 0;
	}
	.guide li::marker {
		color: var(--primary);
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.guide code,
	.content code {
		background: var(--code);
		border-radius: 4px;
		padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
		font-size: 0.9em;
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}
	.guide-note {
		background: var(--accent);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--primary);
		border-radius: 4px;
		padding: 0.6em 1em;
		font-size: 1em !important;
	}
	.guide-table-wrap {
		overflow-x: auto;
		margin: 1em 0;
	}
	.guide-table {
		width: 100%;
		border-collapse: collapse;
		background: var(--accent);
		border-radius: 8px;
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	.guide-table th,
	.guide-table td {
		text-align: left;
		padding: 0.7em 1em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent-light);
	}
	.guide-table th {
		color: var(--primary);
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.guide-table tr:last-child td {
		border-bottom: none;
	}
</style>

<script>
	import '../scripts/reveal.ts';
</script>
